## SECTION 5: FAQ

**Section headline:** Common questions

**Q: What is a remote session?**
A remote session means your technician connects to your device over the internet — with your permission. They can see your screen, move the mouse, and fix the problem directly. It's private, secure, and typically done in 30 minutes or less. No one comes to your home.

**Q: Can I upgrade from Per-Incident to Essentials?**
Yes. After your per-incident session, you can subscribe to Essentials at any time.

**Q: What if my issue isn't fixed?**
*(TBD — confirm policy with Anthony before publishing. Placeholder: "If your issue isn't resolved in the session, we'll work with you to make it right. Details in our Terms of Service.")*

**Q: Is my payment information secure?**
Yes. Payments are processed by Stripe — a PCI-compliant payment processor. Klaravex does not store your card details.

**Q: What devices can you support?**
We support Windows and macOS computers, iPhones, iPads, and Android phones and tablets — for issues that can be addressed remotely. Physical hardware repair is out of scope.

